<title>JAPAN: Honda Motor boosted by weaker yen.</title>
<headline>Honda Motor boosted by weaker yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Honda Motor Corp rose in Tuesday afternoon trade, boosted by a weaker yen against the dollar, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 0600 GMT, the shares were up 20 yen at 2,820 yen with a trade volume of 1.572 million shares.</p>
<p>Brokers said that despite the rounds of profit taking denting the Nikkei average after five continuous days of rises, investors were still interested in buying blue-chip shares expected to do well in the latter half of the fiscal year.</p>
</text>
